{"aggregate_id": "01M2XFT756GZDJR08HS1QZ1XJY", "aggregate_type": "Mission", "event_id": "01M2XFT75ZFY9NDH8KPWBYBCJH", "event_type": "MissionCreated", "payload": {"actor": "stijn@sddevelopment.be", "created_at": "2026-09-19T18:45:45.269021+00:00", "friendly_name": "Terminus-Safety Invariant", "mission_id": "01M2XFT756GZDJR08HS1QZ1XJY", "mission_number": null, "mission_slug": "terminus-safety-invariant-01M2XFT7", "mission_type": "software-dev", "purpose_context": "Today a merge run under the default warn gate mode, or a mission close on an unmerged mission, proceeds past a precondition it never hard-enforced and then fails or fabricates a completion record with no rollback \u2014 wedging in-flight missions and, worse, letting unreviewed code reach the mainline. This mission establishes one terminus-safety invariant across the completion surface so a single mis-timed command can no longer corrupt mission state, protecting the launch walkthrough from unrecoverable dead-ends.", "purpose_tldr": "Completion commands (merge, accept, mission close) must refuse before they mutate, and roll back if a later step fails \u2014 never leaving a mission wedged, split-brain, or falsely completed.", "target_branch": "issue-4764-terminus-safety-invariant", "wp_count": 0}, "project_slug": "spec-kitty", "project_uuid": "8a4a7da6-a97c-4bb4-893a-b31664abfee4", "schema_version": "5.0.0", "timestamp": "2026-09-19T18:45:45.279901+00:00"}
